  "grammar": [
    { "id": "roots", "title": "The root: three consonants, one idea", "concept": "root-pattern", "body": [
      "Most Arabic words are built on a **root** of three consonants. **k-t-b** means writing: katab 'he wrote', ktāb 'book', maktab 'office', maktabe 'library', kātib 'writer', maktūb 'written'.",
      "To find the root, remove prefixes (ma-, mu-, b-, il-), suffixes, and long vowels (ā, ī, ū). What's left is usually the root. This also unlocks Hebrew: כתב k-t-v is the same root."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "الكاتِب كَتَب كْتاب بِالمَكتَبة.", "tr": "il-kātib katab ktāb bil-maktabe.", "en": "The writer wrote a book in the library." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "rt1", "prompt": "What is the root of مَكتَبة (library)?", "answer": "ك-ت-ب", "tr": "k-t-b" },
      { "id": "rt2", "prompt": "What is the root of مَدرَسة (school)?", "answer": "د-ر-س", "tr": "d-r-s" },
      { "id": "rt3", "prompt": "What is the root of مِفتاح (key)?", "answer": "ف-ت-ح", "tr": "f-t-ḥ" },
      { "id": "rt4", "prompt": "What is the root of مَشروب (a drink)?", "answer": "ش-ر-ب", "tr": "sh-r-b" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "patterns", "title": "Patterns: the shape gives the meaning", "concept": "root-pattern", "body": [
      "Write C for each root consonant. Common patterns:",
      "**CāCiC** = the one who does it: kātib (writer), ṭālib (student, 'one who seeks'), sākin (resident).",
      "**maCCaC(a)** = the place where it happens: maktab, maktabe, madrase, maṭʕam (restaurant, from ṭ-ʕ-m 'taste/eat').",
      "**maCCūC** = the thing it was done to: maktūb (written), maftūḥ (opened), mashrūb (drunk → a drink).",
      "**miCCāC** = the tool for it: miftāḥ (key, from f-t-ḥ 'open')."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "المِفتاح بِالمَكتَب، والباب مَفتوح.", "tr": "il-miftāḥ bil-maktab, wil-bāb maftūḥ.", "en": "The key is in the office, and the door is open." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "pa1", "prompt": "Make 'one who writes' from k-t-b.", "answer": "كاتِب", "tr": "kātib" },
      { "id": "pa2", "prompt": "Make 'place of studying' from d-r-s.", "answer": "مَدرَسة", "tr": "madrase" },
      { "id": "pa3", "prompt": "Make 'opened' from f-t-ḥ.", "answer": "مَفتوح", "tr": "maftūḥ" },
      { "id": "pa4", "prompt": "Make 'tool for opening' from f-t-ḥ.", "answer": "مِفتاح", "tr": "miftāḥ" },
      { "id": "pa5", "prompt": "Make 'place of eating' from ṭ-ʕ-m.", "answer": "مَطعَم", "tr": "maṭʕam" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "past", "title": "Past tense: endings after the verb", "concept": "aspect", "body": [
      "The past adds endings: **katab-t** I wrote · **katab-t** you (m) · **katab-ti** you (f) · **katab** he · **katb-it** she · **katab-na** we · **katab-tu** you (pl) · **katab-u** they.",
      "Hollow verbs shorten the vowel with -t: rāḥ 'he went' → **riḥt** 'I went'; shāf → **shift** 'I saw'; nām → **nimt**.",
      "Negate with mā: **mā katabt** = I didn't write."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "رِحت عالجامْعة وشِفت ليلى.", "tr": "riḥt ʕal-jāmʕa w shift Layla.", "en": "I went to the university and saw Layla." },
      { "text": "هِيِّ كَتبِت رِسالة.", "tr": "hiyye katbit risāle.", "en": "She wrote a letter." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "ps1", "prompt": "Say: I went to the market yesterday.", "answer": "رِحت عالسّوق مْبارِح.", "tr": "riḥt ʕas-sūʔ mbāriḥ." },
      { "id": "ps2", "prompt": "Ask a man: What did you do today?", "answer": "شو عْمِلت اليوم؟", "tr": "shū ʕmilt il-yōm?" },
      { "id": "ps3", "prompt": "Say: I ate and then I slept.", "answer": "أَكَلت وبَعدين نِمت.", "tr": "ʔakalt w baʕdēn nimt." },
      { "id": "ps4", "prompt": "Say: I didn't see him.", "answer": "ما شِفتو.", "tr": "mā shifto." },
      { "id": "ps5", "prompt": "Say: We talked with grandma.", "answer": "حَكينا مَع تيتا.", "tr": "ḥakēna maʕ tēta." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "kan", "title": "kān: 'was' (and 'used to')", "concept": "copula-zero", "body": [
      "The present has no 'is', but the past does: **kint** I was · **kint** you (m) · **kinti** you (f) · **kān** he · **kānit** she · **kinna** we · **kāno** they.",
      "**kān fī** = there was. **kān + b-verb** = used to: kint badrus bil-lēl = I used to study at night."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "كِنت بِالبَيت مْبارِح.", "tr": "kint bil-bēt mbāriḥ.", "en": "I was at home yesterday." },
      { "text": "كان في قَهوة طَيِّبة.", "tr": "kān fī ʔahwe ṭayybe.", "en": "There was good coffee." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "kn1", "prompt": "Say: I was at the university yesterday.", "answer": "كِنت بِالجامْعة مْبارِح.", "tr": "kint bil-jāmʕa mbāriḥ." },
      { "id": "kn2", "prompt": "Say: She was happy.", "answer": "كانِت مَبسوطة.", "tr": "kānit mabsūṭa." },
      { "id": "kn3", "prompt": "Say: There was no time.", "answer": "ما كان في وَقت.", "tr": "mā kān fī waʔt." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "possessive", "title": "My, your, his: endings on nouns", "body": [
      "Possession is an ending: **-i** my · **-ak** your (m) · **-ik** your (f) · **-o** his · **-a** her · **-na** our · **-kon** your (pl) · **-hon** their. bēt → bēti, bētak, bēto…",
      "Words ending in ة take a **t** before the ending: ʕēle → **ʕēlti** (my family), sayyāra → **sayyārto** (his car)."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "بَيتي زْغير، بَس بَيتو كْبير.", "tr": "bēti zghīr, bass bēto kbīr.", "en": "My house is small, but his house is big." },
      { "text": "عيلْتي بِأَميركا.", "tr": "ʕēlti b-ʔamērka.", "en": "My family is in America." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "po1", "prompt": "Say: my house", "answer": "بَيتي", "tr": "bēti" },
      { "id": "po2", "prompt": "Say: your (m) book", "answer": "كْتابَك", "tr": "ktābak" },
      { "id": "po3", "prompt": "Say: her mother", "answer": "إمّا", "tr": "imma" },
      { "id": "po4", "prompt": "Say: our family", "answer": "عيلِتنا", "tr": "ʕēlitna" },
      { "id": "po5", "prompt": "Say: My friend is from Lebanon.", "answer": "صاحْبي مِن لُبنان.", "tr": "ṣāḥbi min Libnān." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "idafa", "title": "X of Y: noun + noun (iḍāfa)", "concept": "construct", "body": [
      "'Layla's house' = **bēt Layla** (house Layla). 'The teacher's book' = **ktāb il-mudarris**. The first noun never takes il-.",
      "A first noun ending in ة is said **-it**: jāmʕa → **jāmʕit Hopkins**, maktabe → **maktabit il-jāmʕa**."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "هادا كْتاب المُدَرِّس.", "tr": "hāda ktāb il-mudarris.", "en": "This is the teacher's book." },
      { "text": "مَكتَبِة الجامْعة كْبيرة.", "tr": "maktabit il-jāmʕa kbīre.", "en": "The university library is big." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "id1", "prompt": "Say: Layla's house", "answer": "بَيت ليلى", "tr": "bēt Layla" },
      { "id": "id2", "prompt": "Say: the teacher's book", "answer": "كْتاب المُدَرِّس", "tr": "ktāb il-mudarris" },
      { "id": "id3", "prompt": "Say: the university library", "answer": "مَكتَبِة الجامْعة", "tr": "maktabit il-jāmʕa" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "numbers", "title": "Numbers 1–10 with nouns", "body": [
      "**1**: noun + wāḥad (ktāb wāḥad) or just the noun. **2**: the dual -ēn (ktābēn) or tnēn + plural.",
      "**3–10**: use the short form + plural noun: **tlat** kutub, **ʔarbaʕ** snīn, **khams** līrāt, **ʕashr** daʔāyeʔ.",
      "Prices: b- = 'for': **b-khams līrāt** = for five pounds."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "عِندي تْلات صُفوف وأَربَع اِمتِحانات.", "tr": "ʕindi tlat ṣfūf w ʔarbaʕ imtiḥānāt.", "en": "I have three classes and four exams." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "nm1", "prompt": "Say: two coffees", "answer": "تْنين قَهوة", "tr": "tnēn ʔahwe" },
      { "id": "nm2", "prompt": "Say: three classes", "answer": "تْلات صُفوف", "tr": "tlat ṣfūf" },
      { "id": "nm3", "prompt": "Say: for five pounds", "answer": "بْخَمس لِيرات", "tr": "b-khams līrāt" },
      { "id": "nm4", "prompt": "Say: It's eight o'clock.", "answer": "السّاعة تْمانية.", "tr": "is-sāʕa tmēne." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "article", "title": "il- 'the' and the sun letters", "concept": "definiteness", "body": [
      "'The' is the prefix **il-** (MSA al-). Before 'sun letters' (t th d dh r z s sh ṣ ḍ ṭ ẓ l n), the l sounds like the next letter: **ish-shāy**, **iṭ-ṭālib**, **is-sūʔ**. Before 'moon letters' you hear l: **il-ʔahwe**, **il-ktāb**.",
      "Adjectives copy il-: **il-bēt il-kbīr** = the big house. Without il- on the adjective it's a sentence: **il-bēt kbīr** = the house is big."
    ], "examples": [
